secubox-metablogizer (1.2.3-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * feature: uploads are now versioned back into each site's Gitea repo — every
    /site/{name}/upload auto commits + pushes to origin (git_commit_push),
    serialized under the per-site lock, best-effort (a Gitea failure never fails
    the upload). Response carries a "gitea" status object.
  * postinst: configure the metablogizer service user to push to Gitea's
    internal LXC endpoint (the public host NAT-hairpins and stalls the pack
    transfer).

